{"archetypes":[{"name":"sentinel-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"Checks that the plan's empty-passthrough invariant is consistent with the actual wire-format contract between sentinel writer and all known downstream consumers, and that the new FAILED=true exit paths are handled identically to the existing unusable-sentinel recovery path.","prompt_body":"Verify that the Bash case patterns `*[!0-9]*` and `*[!A-Za-z0-9._-]*` truly do not match the empty string, and that this matches the plan's claim that empty ISSUE_NUMBER/RUN_ID values pass through silently as 'sentinel unusable.' Trace `implement-bootstrap.sh:434`'s AND-chain logic to confirm a new `FAILED=true`+exit-1 from `tracking-issue-read.sh --sentinel` is handled identically to the existing 'unusable sentinel' path and does not introduce an unhandled error branch. Verify that `post-tracking-issue.sh`'s RUN_ID charset (enforced upstream at write time) is a strict subset of `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` so valid sentinel files written by the current writer cannot be rejected by the new reader validation. Check whether any caller of `tracking-issue-read.sh --sentinel` other than the one at `implement-bootstrap.sh:434` exists and would be affected by the new exit paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-mechanics","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Verifies that the new test harness registration, Makefile shard placement, and .md stub format exactly match existing repo conventions to avoid shard-coverage check failures post-merge.","prompt_body":"Inspect the actual Makefile to confirm `test-harnesses-18` exists as a target and that its prerequisite list format matches the plan's description of appending a bare target name. Verify that `test-tracking-issue-read-sentinel` is already registered on `test-harnesses-18` so that co-locating `test-get-issue-state` on the same shard is valid and does not over-fill the shard relative to peers. Check that the `harness-timer.sh` invocation pattern proposed in the plan (`bash scripts/harness-timer.sh $@ bash scripts/test-get-issue-state.sh`) matches at least two existing harness recipes verbatim. Confirm the plan's description of a single long `.PHONY` line matches the Makefile's actual format, since appending to the wrong `.PHONY` block would silently leave the new target out of the phony set. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"case-pattern-charset","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Audits the Bash case glob patterns for charset boundary correctness, especially hyphen placement in bracket expressions and coverage of whitespace/control-character corruption artifacts that are realistic in sentinel files.","prompt_body":"Audit the hyphen position in `*[!A-Za-z0-9._-]*`: confirm it is at the end of the bracket expression (not between two range endpoints), since a misplaced hyphen in a Bash case pattern defines an unintended range rather than a literal hyphen. Verify that tab (0x09) and carriage-return (0x0D) characters — realistic sentinel-file corruption artifacts — are correctly rejected by the pattern and not silently passed through. Check whether the plan's test cases for `test-tracking-issue-read-sentinel.sh` include at least one whitespace input explicitly, or whether that gap leaves the no-whitespace invariant unverified at the harness level. Confirm the plan's `test-get-issue-state.sh` case for `--issue '1 2'` (embedded space) is present and sufficient to cover the same class of inputs for the numeric validator. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
